  "title": "Awesome Skills is a free repo with over 2000 AI agent skills",
  "description": "OpenAI just published the number: the top 10% of companies are six times more likely to use AI skills than everyone else.\n\nFREE REPO - 2,000+ AI agent skills: https://github.com/sickn33/agentic-awesome-skills\n\nSame models. Same prompts. Different setup.\n\nA skill is just a repeatable process, saved. You do the work once, describe how it's done, and your agent repeats it forever instead of you re-explaining it every session. That's the whole gap - it was never talent, and it was never prompt wording.\n\nThe best part is you don't have to write a single one.\n\nThere's a free, open-source repo called Agentic Awesome Skills with over 2,000 skills already built, plus a CLI, a local MCP server and a catalog for browsing them. And if you don't know which one you need, you don't have to read the list - you ask the AI, it scrapes the whole catalog and recommends the one that fits your use case. A library with the librarian built in.\n\nRepo: https://github.com/sickn33/agentic-awesome-skills\n\nWorks with Claude Code, ChatGPT and any agent that reads a skill definition. Start with three that match what you already do every week.\n\n#skills #openai #claudecode #aiagents #github #ai",
  "publishedAt": "2026-09-03T08:03:49Z",
